
Key Concepts
Centralized Storage Layer

Scalable layer holding table data organized by databases and schemas
Built on cloud provider blob storage: S3 (AWS), Azure Blob Storage, or GCP Cloud Storage

Data Ingestion & Format

Data can be loaded via UI, INSERT statements, or COPY INTO <table>
All ingested data is transformed into Snowflake's proprietary columnar format — compressed, encrypted, and optimized for analytics
Both structured and semi-structured data go through the same reorganization process

Post-Ingestion Access

Once loaded, underlying files are fully managed by Snowflake — users have no direct file access
Primary access method: SQL queries
Data can also be exported as CSV, JSON, or Parquet

Micro-Partitions

Snowflake automatically partitions optimized data files into micro-partitions
No static partitioning key required — it's fully automatic
Improves analytical query performance transparently

Stages

Temporary holding areas for data files during the loading process
Covered in depth in the Data Movement section

Billing

Both stages and centralized storage are billed based on cloud provider + region
Flat rate per average terabytes stored per month


